## 👤 User & Admin Management

User accounts live in the `LibreChat` MongoDB database. Standard registrations default to `role: "USER"`.

### 1. Check User Roles
```bash
docker exec -it chat-mongodb mongosh LibreChat --eval 'db.users.find({}, {email: 1, role: 1, _id: 0})'
```

### 2. Grant ADMIN Role
```bash
docker exec -it chat-mongodb mongosh LibreChat --eval 'db.users.updateOne({ email: "user@seedsnet.org" }, { $set: { role: "ADMIN" } })'
```

### 3. Reset User Password
1. Generate a bcrypt hash using the internal node environment:
   ```bash
   docker exec -it AI_Scholar_Hub node -e "console.log(require('bcryptjs').hashSync('NewSecurePassword123!', 10))"
   ```
2. Save the generated hash into MongoDB:
   ```bash
   docker exec -it chat-mongodb mongosh LibreChat --eval 'db.users.updateOne({ email: "user@seedsnet.org" }, { $set: { password: "<INSERT_HASH_HERE>" } })'
   ```

