## 🧠 AIScholarHub Architecture & Vector Pipeline (RAG)

AIScholarHub utilizes a **Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)** pipeline to process uploaded documents, generate vector embeddings, and perform semantic search.


[ User Upload ] ➔ [ Apache Proxy ] ➔ [ LibreChat API ]
│
▼
[ RAG API Service ]
├── Tokenizer / Chunking
├── Embeddings ➔ [ Ollama ]
└── Vector Store ➔ [ Pgvector / ChromaDB ]

```

---

## 🦙 Ollama & Vector Database Integration

Ollama serves as the local LLM and embedding engine, generating vector representations of text without sending data to external APIs.

### 1. Vector Pipeline Components
- **Embedding Model:** Ollama generates embeddings (typically using `nomic-embed-text` or `mxbai-embed-large`).
- **Vector Database:** Embeddings are stored in a vector database (Pgvector or ChromaDB) running as a container in the `docker-compose` network.
- **RAG Engine (`rag_api`):** Accepts file uploads, extracts text, requests embeddings from Ollama, and manages vector collection queries.

### 2. Core Ollama Commands
```bash
# Check running Ollama models inside the container
docker exec -it ollama ollama list

# Pull a required embedding model for vector storage
docker exec -it ollama ollama pull nomic-embed-text

# Pull an inference model
docker exec -it ollama ollama pull llama3

# Test model generation directly inside container
docker exec -it ollama ollama run nomic-embed-text "Test embedding text"

```

